  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I speak for me and a lot of musicians. I realize it might be hard to make but having an option to pick the amount of dB is being caught. Playing a very high note softly on let's say a piano creates around at least -97 dB to be caught in the mic as a sound. So allowing an audio pickup setting setting it to -100 dB will make any sound that is there to be heard also doing will fix cutting out by soft voices and instruments. It's a win-win. ALSO I'd be able to play my piano more clear because when I play soft people complain about cuts and mic shut offs due to low sound and horrible pickup.\n\nThanks,\nPiano.",
